<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Gombe Emirate</h1><p class="st-meta">1804 CE – 1902 CE (approx.) · capital Gombe</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An eastern emirate of the Sokoto Caliphate in north-east Nigeria, founded by Buba Yero on the frontier with Bornu and the Jukun.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Gombe was founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buba-yero">Buba Yero</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulani</a> scholar and warrior who had studied under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usman-dan-fodio">Usman dan Fodio</a> and received a flag from him to wage <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gongola-river">Gongola</a> valley. He began campaigning in 1804, among the first commanders to take the field, and built an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> out of conquests over local peoples on the borders of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kanem-bornu-empire">Kanem-Bornu Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jukun-people">Jukun</a> lands.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buba-yero">Buba Yero</a> ruled until 1841 and pushed his raids far to the south and east, at times clashing with neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirates</a>. Like other emirates, Gombe was ruled by an emir with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulani</a> office-holders, paid tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto</a> and depended on farming, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and the raiding of non-Muslim communities for slaves. The capital moved several times, including to Gombe Abba.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>British forces occupied the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> in 1902, and it became a division of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/protectorate-of-northern-nigeria">Protectorate of Northern Nigeria</a>. The emir remains a traditional ruler, and the modern city of Gombe, founded under colonial rule, is now a state capital.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/gombe-emirate.jpg" alt="Gombe Emirate" width="320" height="161"><figcaption>Image: United States Depart of State, US Embassy to Nigeria · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emir_of_Gombe_Gribbin_2007.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1804 CE – 1902 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Gombe</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Buba Yero</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Fulfulde, Hausa</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/nigeria">Nigeria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Emirate of Gombe</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1853&amp;focus=gombe-emirate" aria-label="Gombe Emirate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4988 1794 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Gombe Emirate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5308 2050L5144 1947M5308 2050L5170 2068"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5144 1947h0M5170 2068h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5308 2050h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5308 2050h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Gombe. <a href="/atlas?year=1853&amp;focus=gombe-emirate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

